Track 2: Resonance Cascades
- Story & Context: During a particularly intense session, Kai "Phaseman" Richter, overwhelmed by the complex interplay of a new granular piano patch and an accelerating orchestral build, inadvertently pushed a master filter too far, causing a feedback loop that filled the vast hall with a beautiful, yet deafening, crystalline wail. He recounted later, his voice hoarse, how for a moment, the sound was so perfect it felt like every atom in his body was singing, almost a confession of his own sonic limits. "This is where the structure starts to sing back at you."
