Track 3: Entropic Jai
- Story & Context: Years after the initial gatherings, an annual pilgrimage to the collider's heart became a ritual, a silent acknowledgment of the energy that had been unleashed, and then gracefully dissipated, into the world. Old Man Tiber, a local who remembered the collider's operational days, would always arrive with a small, hand-carved wooden flute, playing a haunting melody that seemed to mimic the slow decay of the universe, a beautiful acceptance of the inevitable end. "The energy doesn't disappear, it just finds a new dance."
